PHP also has the vulnerability in that $_SESSION is a global.  Thus, PHP apps
co-located on the same web-server can use each other's session state 
between them.  In the natas21-experimenter site, the insecure PHP script
allows you to arbitrarily set key-value pairs.  So, you can set admin=1 on
your session with the experimenter site.  Since $_SESSION is a global,
you can then take the PHPSESSID from the experimenter site and use it
directly on the natas21 site.  It will pull out the session you had on
the experimenter site which had admin set to 1.  The admin parameters are
then dumped out.

